From d0bbb7c7d36bfc784a710b10f52f905fafb47b63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forkmesh <forkmesh@users.forkmesh.local>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 13:34:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/80] Fix rebuild & restart staying stuck waiting on a
 stream/codex session that fails out via processAgentQueue

The stream/codex session-finished handler called processAgentQueue()
last with no recheck afterward. When that call drops the session
straight to Failed (missing repo/checkout/issue) instead of actually
relaunching it, a rebuild queued behind the run never gets its final
recheck and stays stuck on "Waiting for running actions to finish"
even though the fleet has gone idle. onAgentFinished (the legacy
AgentRunner completion path) already guards this exact case (adhoc
#75); mirror the same maybeStartQueuedRebuild() call here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 qt_client/src/MainWindowAgents.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/qt_client/src/MainWindowAgents.cpp b/qt_client/src/MainWindowAgents.cpp
index 3649961a..b7bc83f1 100644
--- a/qt_client/src/MainWindowAgents.cpp
+++ b/qt_client/src/MainWindowAgents.cpp
@@ -5731,6 +5731,14 @@ void MainWindow::startCliTranscript(AgentSession &session, const Issue &issue,
             showAgentSession(sid);
