From 10a2f41d8d8f55dba5c8e8d0adae7cb0f70971b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forkmesh <forkmesh@users.forkmesh.local>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 13:51:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/80] Branches: advance to next branch after Merge to main

A clean "Merge to main" from the Branches view left the just-merged
branch selected, so the panel re-rendered its now-empty diff - reading
as "the whole page refreshed." Steer the re-select logic at the
neighbouring branch instead (like the post-delete flow, adhoc #256), so
merging walks down the list. Only for the non-destructive Branches-view
button; the Worktrees/Agents merge flows that delete the branch keep
their own handling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
