From 9cf99827a4ec78cbb9636dcd8eabcc7682d50944 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forkmesh <forkmesh@users.forkmesh.local>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 15:11:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 21/80] Avoid committerdate branch sort on agent-session
 selection

updateAgentFilesTabState() ran repoBranches() on every agent-session
click, which shells out to `git branch --sort=-committerdate`. That sort
reads every branch's tip commit and stalled the UI ~500 ms on the
forkmesh repo, which accumulates hundreds of self-merged agent branches
(adhoc #150).

The button-state logic only needs the base branch name to decide whether
a session sits on a feature branch. Add repoDefaultBranchFast(), which
trusts a configured default outright and otherwise resolves it from an
unsorted `git for-each-ref` (ref-name enumeration only, no commit reads),
and use it in the hot selection path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
