Every git-info-refs through the host DO ran _state_pins, which for mirror
namespaces re-scanned the whole repositories table and decrypt_row()'d
every row, plus read the entire repo_state_history table — per request.
Under a clone burst this held the single Worker event loop long enough
for the runtime to cancel concurrent requests as hung ("RuntimeError:
Cannot enter into task ..."), the same failure family as adhoc #144,
which memoized the neighbouring _online_source_of_truth scan on this
exact path but left this one.

- Group-source records now come from the shared 5s per-isolate
  _decrypted_public_catalog memo (public + active-node scoped; a group
  source invisible to the memo just falls back to the target's own
  pins, the pre-existing legacy behaviour).
- The repo_state_history SELECT is scoped to the target + same-group
  source keys, mirroring the /mirrors payload's earlier scoping fix,
  instead of reading every repo's pin history.

