Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

forkmesh.com/ is now served by a new, tiny JS Worker (forkmesh-marketing,
cloudflare_marketing_worker/) while forkmesh.com/<anything> stays on the
existing relay Worker (forkmesh-relay). The split is done with an exact-match
Cloudflare route on "forkmesh.com/" — routes rank by specificity and beat a
Worker Custom Domain, so only the root URL moves; every other path, including
the landing page's own CSS/JS/asset subresources, keeps resolving to the relay.

- The landing document stays canonical in cloudflare_worker/public/index.html;
  the marketing wrangler [build] step copies it in (public/ there is generated
  and gitignored), so the page cannot drift between the two Workers.
- entry.js mirrors the relay's / semantics: forkmesh_session=1 -> 302
  /dashboard with no-store; otherwise the landing page with no-cache +
  Vary: cookie, streamed straight from the asset store. Being a JS Worker also
  takes the highest-traffic route off the Pyodide isolate's hot path.
- Every marketing response stamps x-forkmesh-worker: marketing; its deploy.sh
  (which shares CLOUDFLARE_* creds from the relay's .env.production) polls the
  live root for that header and fails loudly if the route never took effect.
- The relay keeps its homepage handler and "/" worker-first entry as the
  fallback for workers.dev previews and local dev (commented in wrangler.toml).
- tests/test_marketing_worker.py pins the contract: exact-root-only route,
  single-source index.html, mirrored / semantics, relay fallback intact.

