+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nTurn the existing signed receive-pack path into a normal user workflow without persisting short-lived credentials in repository configuration.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Add one shared helper that creates the correct owner or delegated-write canonical, timestamp, signature, and authenticated push URL.\n- Expose a desktop action that either performs the push or copies an exact one-shot command, with a separate headless command using the same helper.\n- Never write the signed password into `.git/config`, shell history instructions, logs, crash reports, or diagnostics.\n- Refresh an expired credential once after a clear authentication challenge; do not retry authorization failures indefinitely.\n- Distinguish offline source, invalid identity, insufficient role, expired signature, ref-policy denial, and receive-pack failure.\n- Remove stale user-facing copy and comments that still say relay push is unavailable.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Owner and delegated writers can push from desktop and headless flows.\n- Read-only users receive a clear denial before any ref changes.\n- Secret-bearing URLs are redacted everywhere and are not persisted.\n- Expiry refresh is bounded and never changes the intended remote or refspec.\n- Successful pushes trigger the existing integrity re-attestation path.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nDepends on #435.\n\n## Verification\n\nAdd helper, UI, redaction, expiry, role, offline-source, and successful-push tests using the receive-pack scenarios from #435.",
