+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nProvide a reproducible, non-interactive service install that can be monitored, stopped cleanly, backed up, restored, and verified before use.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Add a checked-in service-manager unit template plus install, uninstall, start, stop, and status commands around existing headless mode.\n- Run as an unprivileged account with explicit configuration, identity, mirror, and log directories.\n- Add a health command that verifies process state, relay connectivity, and readability of configured mirrors.\n- Implement graceful shutdown with a bounded timeout and clear recovery after an unclean stop.\n- Add a cold-backup manifest with relative paths, sizes, and checksums plus restore validation into an empty target directory.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Runtime requires no display server and does not run as root.\n- Mutable data lives only in documented directories.\n- Backup output never prints key material and detects checksum mismatch.\n- Restore rejects unsafe permissions, corrupt manifests, and non-empty targets.\n- CI installs the service in a temporary root, starts a fixture node, checks health, stops it, restores a backup, and reads the restored mirror.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nNone.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun install/uninstall idempotency, unprivileged execution, health, graceful and forced stop, backup consistency, corrupt restore, and restored-mirror tests.",
