+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nGuarantee standard Git interoperability with a matrix generated entirely by executable probes through real repository-serving paths.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Probe full clone, fetch, remote management, authenticated push, protected and unprotected force-push, branch and tag deletion, shallow clone, partial clone, submodules, bundles, signed commits, signed push certificates, local hooks, and unchanged third-party Git porcelain behavior.\n- Delegate standard large-object probes to #467 and dependency-client probes to #455 while including their results in the same generated matrix.\n- After each accepted write, clone again and assert exact refs and object identifiers.\n- Emit a stable compatibility report with probe identifier, pass or fail, tested commit, route, and concise diagnostic.\n- Render documentation only from the report and retain no handwritten capability claims.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Every roadmap compatibility row is passing by the August 1 release gate; unsupported is allowed only as an in-sprint diagnostic and blocks release.\n- Authorized writes, unauthorized rejection, protected-ref rejection, and post-write cloneability are proven.\n- Partial, shallow, submodule, bundle, hook, signature, large-object, and dependency behavior each have an offline fixture.\n- A previously passing probe regression fails continuous integration.\n- No probe requires a live external service or personal credential.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nDepends on #434; consumes #441, #455, and #467 before release closure.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun the matrix twice against fresh repositories and standard client subprocesses, compare normalized reports and object ids, and inject one regression per operation family.",
