+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nLet people read without an account and submit signed issues, comments, reviews, and pull requests from a browser identity that can later move to a full node.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Generate an Ed25519 contribution identity in the browser and keep the encrypted private material in local protected storage.\n- Add passkey, standards-based identity-provider, and email magic-link session adapters without making any one adapter mandatory.\n- Queue signed contributions offline and submit them through the existing bounded inbox when connectivity returns.\n- Provide an explicit export and handoff flow into the recoverable identity model in #447.\n- Keep anonymous access read-only and apply existing rate, size, signature, and attachment validation before inbox storage.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A clean browser can submit each supported contribution without installing a node.\n- Private signing material never reaches logs, analytics, URLs, or server storage.\n- Offline replay is idempotent and preserves the original signed bytes.\n- Identity handoff retains authorship and revokes the abandoned browser device when requested.\n- Anonymous mutation attempts and invalid sessions fail without creating inbox state.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nUses the existing signed contribution inbox; coordinates identity upgrade with #447.\n\n## Verification\n\nExercise anonymous reads, each sign-in adapter, browser-key creation, offline queue/replay, duplicate submission, handoff, revocation, rate limits, and secret-leak scans in browser tests.",
