+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nMake personal and organization identities auditable across device loss, key rotation, maintainer delegation, and recovery.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Support passkey and hardware-authenticator enrollment, multiple devices, named device revocation, and recovery-code fallback.\n- Define signed rotation records that bind old and new keys, reject rollback, and retain historical signature verification.\n- Add N-of-M social recovery with time delay, cancellation, and an auditable recovery event.\n- Represent organization actors as threshold-managed keysets with scoped delegated maintainers.\n- Add timestamped external-account proofs and trust scopes for maintenance, review, mirroring, release signing, and security contact roles.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Lost-device recovery never lets one recovery participant take control alone.\n- Revoked keys cannot author new accepted events but continue to verify historical events.\n- Organization threshold and delegation changes are signed, versioned, and replay-safe.\n- Trust in one scope never grants another scope.\n- Rotation, recovery, and proof fixtures converge in desktop, browser, and relay validation.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nBuilds on browser handoff in #446 and the native signed-event rules in #440.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun device-add/remove, hardware-authenticator, N-of-M recovery, canceled recovery, rotation, rollback, organization threshold, delegation expiry, and scoped-proof vectors.",
