+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nUse the existing archive cryptography in the production private-repository path so Git objects, collaboration data, artifacts, indexes, caches, and backups are encrypted at rest.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Wire streaming seal and open operations into private mirror publish, fetch, serve, backup, and restore paths.\n- Encrypt issue, pull-request, review, release, and room metadata with the same repository visibility boundary.\n- Build local search from an encrypted index or an explicitly active decrypted workspace; never publish private terms to the public catalog.\n- Use versioned recipient envelopes for people, devices, recovery keys, and organization-managed keys.\n- Keep catalog entries opaque except for the minimum routing fields required to locate authorized ciphertext.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Known private plaintext is absent from mirror storage, cache, index, logs, crash reports, and backups outside an explicitly active decrypted workspace.\n- Streaming paths do not buffer a full repository or artifact in memory.\n- Unauthorized peers cannot distinguish private object names, collaboration subjects, or search terms.\n- Corrupt envelopes and ciphertext fail before destination state changes.\n- Public repository behavior and performance remain unchanged.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nUses the existing mirror cryptography primitives; key lifecycle continues in #449.\n\n## Verification\n\nPublish and clone a private fixture with code, issues, reviews, releases, artifacts, and searchable terms, then scan all inactive storage and diagnostic output for the seeded plaintext markers.",
