+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nLet each operator decide locally what the node fetches, stores, serves, indexes, rate-limits, quarantines, or removes without creating a network-global deletion mechanism.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Define a versioned local policy for repository size, visibility, file classes, large objects, artifacts, maintainer scopes, peer and repository allowlists or blocklists, storage quotas, and request rates.\n- Evaluate policy before fetch, after object inspection, before advertisement, and before serving.\n- Import signed community policy lists only after local approval and retain their source, version, expiry, and scope.\n- Add an operator-local report and removal-request inbox with quarantine, unlist, block, purge-local-copy, and dismiss actions.\n- Provide dry-run decisions, stable reason codes, bounded audit records, and defaults matching current behavior.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Policy denial never leaves advertised partial data.\n- Rate limits bound storage, CPU, and network work per untrusted peer.\n- Community lists never override local policy automatically.\n- Reports and removal requests cannot trigger action on another operator's node.\n- Policy changes are atomic and explain every affected repository with no secret content in logs.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nScanner outcomes from #451 feed this policy; no external policy service is required.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun pre-fetch, post-inspection, advertisement, serving, rate-limit, blocklist, community-list, report-inbox, quarantine, and local-purge scenarios against public and private fixtures.",
