+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nUse one bounded scanner across local hooks, publication, and mirror intake so risky content is caught before replication whenever possible.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Create a shared scanner interface for secret fingerprints, private-key formats, malware rules, and operator-supplied detectors.\n- Provide opt-in pre-commit hook installation plus mandatory configurable pre-push or pre-publish evaluation.\n- Scan newly fetched public objects before a mirror advertises them and quarantine failures through #450.\n- Log only rule identifiers, fingerprints, paths, and locations; never log matching secret bytes.\n- Require an explicit signed local override and show that redaction cannot be guaranteed after data has replicated.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The same fixture produces the same decision in hook, publish, and mirror paths.\n- Private ciphertext is not mis-scanned before authorized decryption.\n- A clean replacement clears quarantine only after a complete rescan.\n- Overrides are scoped, expiring, auditable, and cannot silently disable other rules.\n- Scanner time, memory, file count, and object size are bounded for hostile input.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nIntegrates with the node-local policy engine in #450.\n\n## Verification\n\nSeed secret, malware, binary, oversized, renamed, deleted, encrypted, overridden, and cleaned fixtures through each entry point and scan all diagnostics for the original match bytes.",
