+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nKeep repositories and collaboration usable on unreliable links by syncing only the requested data and resuming verified transfer work.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Add full, default-branch, collaboration-only, blobless, and metadata-first sync profiles.\n- Allow large objects, release assets, non-default branches, and history beyond a depth boundary to be deferred independently.\n- Apply per-node upload and download caps with a token bucket shared by Git, collaboration, and artifact transfer.\n- Persist verified chunk or object checkpoints so interrupted transfers resume without retransmitting completed work.\n- Show estimated, completed, deferred, and remaining bytes plus an exact explanation of unavailable content.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Every profile advertises only content it can actually serve.\n- Resumption verifies prior bytes and rejects mismatched checkpoints.\n- Collaboration-only sync transfers no Git blob or release-asset payload.\n- Changing profiles fetches the minimal missing data without rebuilding existing verified state.\n- Bandwidth limits remain within a deterministic tolerance in tests.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nUses Git probes from #435, offline manifests from #441, and the large-object path in #467.\n\n## Verification\n\nInterrupt every profile at multiple byte boundaries, resume it, change profiles, corrupt a checkpoint, and verify object identifiers, advertised coverage, byte accounting, and rate bounds.",
