+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nConfigure and diagnose direct, proxy, overlay, and LAN-only repository routes without silently exposing a direct network path.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Define route adapters with address, remote-name-resolution, authentication reference, expected privacy mode, and priority.\n- Probe each route for reachability, latency, clone capability, last success, and a sanitized failure reason.\n- Support proxy-only and LAN-only modes that disable direct DNS resolution and direct sockets at the lowest shared transport layer.\n- Allow simultaneous route publication while making the selected route and any fallback policy explicit.\n- Expose route health through one contract consumed by desktop, browser, headless health, and #466.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Proxy-only and LAN-only leak tests observe no direct DNS query or socket attempt.\n- No route silently falls back to a less private mode.\n- Authentication material and full private addresses never enter diagnostics.\n- Health changes update live without restarting the node.\n- A stock Git clone uses the selected healthy route or returns its exact bounded failure reason.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nNearby discovery and peer streams are added in #472; availability consumes this contract in #466.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun simultaneous healthy, slow, failed, misconfigured, credential-rejected, name-resolution, proxy-only, LAN-only, and explicit-fallback route fixtures with socket-level leak assertions.",
