+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nPackage the headless node as a reproducible rootless OCI image with one-command seed startup and explicit durable state.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Build the image from the same headless binary and directory contract as #442.\n- Run as a numeric unprivileged user with read-only application layers and explicit identity, mirror, configuration, and log volumes.\n- Provide a declarative single-node configuration with health checks, resource limits, restart behavior, and graceful shutdown.\n- Pin build inputs and emit an image digest, software bill of materials, and provenance attestation.\n- Add upgrade and rollback checks that preserve durable data and reject incompatible schema downgrades.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The image never requires root or a display server.\n- Deleting and recreating the runtime preserves only documented volumes.\n- A clean command starts a seed, passes health, serves a fixture clone, and stops cleanly.\n- The same source commit produces reproducible application contents.\n- Upgrade failure leaves the prior verified runtime and data usable.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nConsumes the service and storage contract from #442; platform variants continue in #473.\n\n## Verification\n\nBuild from a clean dependency cache, start the declarative fixture, clone through it, restart, upgrade, inject an incompatible schema, roll back, and verify volume ownership and cleanup.",
