+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nKeep cloning, mirroring, contributing, identity, and self-hosting independent of optional account-service modules.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Move optional account extensions behind explicit versioned interfaces and disabled-by-default feature flags.\n- Remove optional-service fields and calls from required repository creation, node startup, identity, clone, push, and contribution paths.\n- Namespace optional schemas, routes, migrations, and UI so the core can build and run with the module absent.\n- Provide a reversible migration for existing optional records without changing repository identities or signed collaboration history.\n- Generate core documentation and API schemas from a build in which optional modules are not present.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Core desktop, browser, headless, relay, and self-host tests pass with the optional module physically absent.\n- No required API response or signed repository object contains an optional-module field.\n- Enabling or disabling the module does not change Git or collaboration object identifiers.\n- Migration is idempotent and preserves user-controlled exports.\n- Core onboarding contains no optional-service detour.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nNone.\n\n## Verification\n\nBuild and run the complete core portfolio with the module absent, disabled, enabled, migrated, and removed again; compare repository identities, signed event bytes, API schemas, and onboarding steps.",
