+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nMake discovery signals portable signed objects whose visibility and trusted indexes are chosen by each user.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Define star, watch, bookmark, follow, recommend, mirror, production-use, and security-review assertion events.\n- Include subject identity, optional evidence, visibility scope, creation, expiry, and undo references in the signed schema.\n- Derive watch notifications and aggregate counts through deterministic folds without treating popularity as trust.\n- Allow private local bookmarks, shared assertions, portable export and import, and user-selected trusted index sources.\n- Deduplicate replayed events and preserve conflicting independent opinions.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Undo and expiry remove an assertion from current state without erasing history.\n- Private assertions never enter public catalog or notification payloads.\n- Imported assertions retain original signatures and source provenance.\n- Index selection changes aggregation without changing the underlying records.\n- Shuffled and duplicated event sets converge across clients.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nUses convergence rules from #440 and identity scopes from #447.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun every assertion, visibility, evidence, expiry, undo, import, duplicate, conflicting-opinion, trusted-index, and derived-notification fixture through all folds and renderers.",
