+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nDeliver bounded signed repository events to operator-configured HTTP consumers with reliable retry and privacy controls.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Define a versioned envelope for push, issue, pull request, review, check, release, mirror, policy, and availability events.\n- Support endpoint and event allowlists, secret references, signature rotation, and a verification challenge.\n- Assign stable delivery identifiers and persist bounded retry, exponential backoff, cancellation, and dead-letter state.\n- Redact or omit private repository payloads according to endpoint scope before signing the delivery envelope.\n- Expose per-delivery status, attempts, next retry, response class, and replay action without storing response secrets.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Duplicate attempts are idempotent at the fixture consumer.\n- A failing endpoint cannot block repository writes or other endpoints.\n- Private fields never reach a public-scoped endpoint.\n- Retry and dead-letter storage are bounded by count, bytes, and age.\n- Every delivered envelope verifies independently against its configured signer.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nUses deterministic event records from #440; inbound checks and replayable streams are separate in #471.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun success, timeout, disconnect, retry-after, duplicate, invalid challenge, key rotation, private redaction, dead-letter, manual replay, and storage-bound fixtures.",
