+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nShow how far each repository, issue, pull request, comment, review, release, and revision has propagated using verifiable receipts rather than optimistic client state.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Define a signed receipt keyed by object kind, object identifier, revision hash, node identity, seen, verified, pinned, timestamp, expiry, and trust scope.\n- Aggregate known, seen, verified, pinned, trusted, stale, and rejected counts with a configurable success quorum.\n- Keep receipt replay idempotent and fold shuffled independent receipts deterministically.\n- Expose concise per-object status and the evidence timestamp in desktop, browser, mobile, and headless output.\n- Protect private object names and participant identities with scoped opaque identifiers.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A receipt counts only after its signature, object revision, trust scope, and expiry verify.\n- Old receipts never count for a new revision.\n- Quorum thresholds produce identical results on every node.\n- Private receipts reveal no repository or collaboration title to an unauthorized observer.\n- Disconnect, reconnect, repin, corruption, and repair update status without restart.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nUses deterministic folding from #440 and feeds repository availability in #439 and #466.\n\n## Verification\n\nShuffle, duplicate, expire, forge, revoke trust, revise objects, disconnect, reconnect, pin, unpin, corrupt, and repair receipt fixtures across every supported object kind.",
