+            "body": "## Outcome\n\nSerialize ready pull requests into protected refs using signed merge, squash, or rebase strategies with exact-head revalidation.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Define signed enqueue, reorder, pause, retry, cancel, and result events with deterministic concurrent ordering.\n- Rebuild the candidate against the latest protected base and rerun required ownership, review, and workflow checks.\n- Implement merge, squash, and rebase strategies with a signed resulting commit or attestation and explicit author or committer mapping.\n- Update the protected ref atomically only if the base, head, policy, and check set still match.\n- Pause conflicts with a browser and command-line resolution path that creates a new patchset rather than mutating history.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Concurrent enqueue events produce the same queue order on every node.\n- Stale base, head, approval, check, policy, or identity state prevents the ref update.\n- Every strategy produces the expected tree and a verifiable signed result.\n- One failed item does not discard or reorder unrelated queued work.\n- A conflict cannot be bypassed without a reviewed replacement patchset or authorized signed override.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nDepends on #437, #454, #468, #470, and #471.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun concurrent enqueue, all strategies, base movement, head rewrite, stale checks, revoked reviewer, policy update, conflict and resolution, cancellation, retry, override, crash recovery, and atomic-ref fixtures.",
